# prompt: laser charging up, rising whine
# tags: laser, charge, rise, whine
# A charge is the one laser sound whose envelope opens slowly — the attack is
# the charging, and a percussive one would read as a shot instead. Both layers
# sweep together, so the resonance climbs with the pitch rather than sitting
# still and filtering it.
sound "laser charge" 300ms laser
  whine: chirp saw ~300Hz[150..600] -> 2400Hz in 240ms >> bp ~1800Hz[800..4000] Q4 | gain 0.4 attack 40ms decay 250ms
  hum: tone tri ~150Hz[80..320] -> 600Hz in 240ms | gain 0.2 attack 50ms decay 240ms
